{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>His linen tunic.</b> It is the כֻּתֹּנֶת. And what does מִדּוֹ teach? That it should be to his measure (there)." "<b>On his flesh.</b> That nothing should interpose in between (Zevachim 19)." "<b>And he shall lift up the ashes.</b> He would scoop a full pan from the inner consumed parts and place it on the east side of the ramp (Tamid 28)." "<b>The ashes that the fire has consumed of the burnt offering.</b> And it has turned to ash — from that ash he lifts up a תְּרוּמָה <b>and place it beside the altar.</b>" "<b>On the altar.</b> If he found limbs that had not yet been consumed, he returns them onto the altar — after he has swept coals this way and that and taken from the inner parts, as it says: ״אֶת הָעֹלָה עַל הַמִּזְבֵּחַ״."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:11.888153070Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}